  "diagnosis_text": "**Diagnosis: the s1\u2013s3 inter-switch link is down.**\n\nEvidence:\n- `h1 \u2192 h5` ICMP fails completely: **3/3 packets lost**.\n- `h1` can still reach local peer `h2`, and `h5` can reach local peer `h6`, so the two host-facing access segments are working.\n- Other remote traffic from `s3` also fails (`h1 \u2192 h3`, `h2 \u2192 h5`), localising the outage to connectivity leaving `s3`, rather than h1 or h5 specifically.\n- The configured `s1:2 \u2194 s3:1` link is absent from ONOS\u2019s active-link view.\n- Both ends are administratively/operationally disabled:\n  - `s3` port **1** (`s3-eth1`, peer `s1:2`): `enabled: false`\n  - `s1` port **2** (`s1-eth2`, peer `s3:1`): `enabled: false`\n\nThere is also a forwarding consequence: s3\u2019s installed baseline flows send traffic for h5 (and other remote hosts) to **port 1**, and ARP from h1 is likewise forwarded toward port 1. Since that port is down, those frames are discarded. Although alternate physical paths via `s2`/`s4` exist and their ports appear up, the currently installed forwarding rules are not using them.\n\n**Fault localisation:** the failed/disabled segment is **s3-eth1 \u2194 s1-eth2**. Restoring that link, or updating/recomputing the forwarding policy to use an active alternate path, is required; I cannot make that change from here.",
